From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: gc8613: give the sensor time to boot

The GC8613 does not answer on I2C 20 ms after reset release on the T41;
the probe fails reading the chip ID with -EIO. Wait 100 ms before the
first register access.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/gc8613.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc8613.c
@@ -604,7 +604,7 @@
 	/* The sensor needs MCLK while reset is released. */
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(gc8613->powerdown_gpio, 0);
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(gc8613->reset_gpio, 0);
-	msleep(20);
+	msleep(100);
 
 	return 0;
 
